The '''2024 European Parliament elections''' in France were held on 9 June 2024, as part of the [[2024 European Parliament election]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=European elections 2024 |url=https://multimedia.europarl.europa.eu/package/european-elections-2024_23001 |access-date=2023-10-15 |website=European Parliament Multimedia Centre |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
The [[Borne government]] lost its majority in the [[2022 French legislative election]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2022-06-19 |title=French elections: Macron loses majority as French vote fragments |language=en-GB |work=[[BBC News]] |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-61859881 |access-date=2023-10-15}}</ref>

== Electoral system ==
A bill creating a [[France (European Parliament constituency)|single national constituency]] was approved by the [[National Assembly (France)|National Assembly]] in a vote on the first reading on 20 February 2018,<ref name="scrutin-AN">{{cite web |date=20 February 2018 |title=Analyse du scrutin n° 407 - Deuxième séance du 20/02/2018 |url=http://www2.assemblee-nationale.fr/scrutins/detail/(legislature)/15/(num)/407 |access-date=1 June 2018 |publisher=[[Assemblée nationale]]}}</ref> and the Senate officially adopted the bill on 23 May 2018,<ref name="scrutin-Senat">{{cite web |date=23 May 2018 |title=Scrutin n° 104 - séance du 23 mai 2018 |url=https://www.senat.fr/scrutin-public/2017/scr2017-104.html |access-date=1 June 2018 |publisher=[[Sénat]]}}</ref> which was promulgated on 25 June after its validation by the [[Constitutional Council (France)|Constitutional Council]].<ref>{{cite web |date=25 June 2018 |title=LOI n° 2018-509 du 25 juin 2018 relative à l'élection des représentants au Parlement européen (1) |url=https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/affichTexte.do?cidTexte=JORFTEXT000037102048 |access-date=25 July 2018 |publisher=[[Légifrance]]}}</ref>

French members of the [[European Parliament]] are elected through a [[Closed list|closed list proportional representation]] system.

=== Apportionment ===
{{See also|Apportionment in the European Parliament}}
When the [[Brexit withdrawal agreement|United Kingdom left the European Union]] in January 2020, 46 of Britain's 73 seats were abolished and 27 seats were reapportioned to other countries.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2017-04-26 |title=Italian proposal for who gets British MEP seats |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/italian-proposal-for-who-gets-british-mep-seats/ |access-date=2022-09-09 |website=[[POLITICO]] |language=en-US}}</ref> As a result, the total number of MEPs decreased from 751 seats to 705.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2017-09-07 |title=MEPs propose cut in their ranks after Brexit |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/the-incredible-shrinking-european-parliament/ |access-date=2022-09-09 |website=[[POLITICO]] |language=en-US}}</ref> 

For the 2024 election, the [[European Parliament]] was increased to 720 MEPs with France receiving two new seats.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-07-28 |title=European Parliament set to grow by 15 MEPs in 2024 |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/eu-parliament-mep-election-2024/ |access-date=2024-01-25 |website=[[POLITICO]] |language=en}}</ref>

